parts+=['## Stage 2: generalized shared pattern','Given a Cartesian graph z=g(x,y) over an explicitly bounded rectangle and a polynomial scalar f, determine only the missing repeated-integral integrand f(x,y,g(x,y))√(1+g_x²+g_y²). Formal partial differentiation, substitution, metric construction and polynomial multiplication are the assessed operations. The differential order is dy dx. There is one fixed worked solution independent of the learner choice.','## Stage 3: components and complete bank mapping','The tables above map all 40 original options to their original owned UUID, correct designation where present, exact value and parameterized raw recipe. Each profile `raw:q-N` comprises the entire five-member original bank. A scalar multiplier k/k₀ scales f and every scalar solution/choice row without changing g or the derivative metric. This is a conservative parameterized structural generalization, not a recovered explanation of unusual exponent errors. Surface changes are rejected in these opaque raw profiles. The observed original expression trees are parsed, scaled and rendered through public generate; there is no source-payload return branch or final answer lookup. Original spelling is recovered per complete expression slot only when its symbolic value equals the original component.','No bank member is individually replaced or selected from a distractor pool. The normal complete `measure_conversion` bank is selected first and then evaluates precisely `[P M, P, P M², P/M, P√(g_x²+g_y²)]`, where P=f(x,y,g) and M=√(1+g_x²+g_y²). The mistakes are omission of surface measure, failure to take its square root, inversion of the measure conversion, and omission of the graph metric’s leading 1. Each is a real operation on the displayed formula. Native UUID tests independently check all five choices, while symbolic readback checks their displayed complete mathematical values. Any equivalence or invalid domain rejects the whole instance.','Historical bank domain anomalies remain explicit: q-161321 has √(5x) on x∈[-1,1]; q-161314 has √(3x) on x∈[-1,1]; q-161325 has 1+16x²−4y² and 1+4x²−4y² inside wrong radicals, becoming negative at x=0,y=2. q-161323’s √(5x) is real on its original x∈[0,1], but its missing grading metadata and arbitrary mixed exponents remain unresolved. These raw banks are all evidence-only; none enters default sampling. The correct inferred q-161323 expression is −3√10(x²+xy). Its first historical option equals this expression, but absent original correct designation is never counted as matched.','## Stage 4: reusable masks and bounded domains','Observed easy masks have g=ax^m+by^n and f=kx^u y^v z^w, with exponent patterns exactly as cataloged in classification. Default nonzero a,b,k∈{−2,−1,1,2,−√2,√2}; the original exact values are included. The original bounds all fit the domain: integer endpoints of magnitude ≤3, lower<upper on each coordinate. The raw masks permit k/k₀∈{−3,−2,−1,1,2,3} and hold a,b fixed; they preserve each original derivative block, whole row count, row order, punctuation and prose. Normal records retain formal operator rows plus generic formula, substituted derivative metric, unsimplified actual substitution, expanded product and repeated-integral setup. No diagnosis text is invented.','Authored moderate templates coupled_xz/coupled_yz use g=ax²+bxy+cy² and f=kxz or kyz. Both partials contain two nonzero algebraic terms and there is exactly one substantive z substitution with a three-term product. Authored hard templates coupled_two_x/coupled_two_y use f=kxz+lyz² or kyz+lxz² with the same graph. There are exactly two z substitutions, one square of a three-term graph and two outer polynomial products before collection. Their degrees differ, so the two assessed f terms cannot cancel each other. A cross coefficient in the expanded square can cancel; the required square/substitution workload remains unchanged. All nonzero authored coefficients have signed magnitude ≤2, enforced identically on samplers and explicit calls. All templates within either authored level are unordered coordinate placements.','Meaningful variety: easy provides 6×6×6=216 coefficient tuples per observed shape before mathematical deduplication; moderate 4⁴=256 tuples per coordinate placement; hard 4⁵=1024 tuples per placement. Bounds are excluded from task counts. Coefficient sign symmetries and proportional expressions can reduce equivalent assessed outputs; these raw tuple counts are not claimed as unique question counts. Mathematical fingerprints canonicalize actual f(g) and the squared derivative metric; complete banks, prose, profile labels, coefficient spellings and seed are excluded. Content identity separately includes actual difficulty, prompt, fixed solution and complete bank with correct designations, excluding option order and seed.','The raw source key-presence parity is checked independently for every record. q-161323 preserves its AAAAAAA placeholder and original strange integral spelling; a completed normal plane_xz question is separately authored and eligible. It has the normal displayed empty box, full solution and independent mathematical correct choice. No TeX escape repair is claimed on the basis of JSON serialization.']
